      "assistant_text": "According to the [[write-journal]] page, it describes **how the guarded write path journals prior file state for rollback on failure**.\n\nSpecifically, the page explains that before the guarded tool executor overwrites any file, it records that file\u0027s prior state \u2014 either its previous content (if it existed) or the fact that it didn\u0027t exist \u2014 into an in-memory write journal. If the agent run fails for any reason (turn cap exceeded, unrecoverable error, or denied writes), the journal can roll every recorded write back in reverse order: restoring previous content for files that existed, and deleting newly created files. This mechanism provides all-or-nothing semantics for writes without requiring a database transaction \u2014 the journal itself serves as the transaction log, held in memory for the duration of one run.\n\nThe page also notes that the Query agent never uses the rollback path since it has no write tool at all.",
